#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a47b88ad-e6a3-548e-b3a7-95ede04a074e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288553} {:answer/id #uuid "28e902a6-5051-5cca-b30e-0fee2f148317" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288554} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b15967-d3ef-551a-947f-bfb28904e4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288555} {:answer/id #uuid "debcc437-3577-57c9-b607-c2c9c289e770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288556} {:answer/id #uuid "4e80adb5-d2d0-5375-ac8e-96c908f4c86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e80adb5-d2d0-5375-ac8e-96c908f4c86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288557} :answer-field/id #uuid "3906e258-840c-5de5-af0e-44d141899def" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "760ba6ba-f519-5e68-b2c7-ade22689c6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18284" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $-16.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22}=\\frac{1}{-16}\\cdot 4=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
